Z||000000||GT-maniac||04-15-2001||11:08 AM||||Now before everybody gets all excited I did do a search on this topic and came to the conclusion that I'm probably looking at replacing my gear select cable. But before I spend $ 150 on a new cable I'd like to be more sure. The problem is the car won't go into reverse or the. Also it's really difficult to get going in all the other gears. Even when I'm in first it feels like I'm trying to start off in 3rd or the. I have to really feather the clutch to get going. It does seem to go through the gears fairly easily though. I can push the selector up and down a bit at the transmission but it doesn't move much and doesn't seem to put it into reverse. Anybody have any ideas ?<BR>The car is an 87 GT with the 5 speed.  ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-15-2001||07:29 PM||||Hey GT!<BR>Before you spend your money, have a friend shift through the gears while you watch the cables at the trans...<BR>I had a clip that holds the shift cable come off and cause a similar problem...<BR>$1.00 for a clip or $150 for a cable...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||04-15-2001||09:24 PM||||Ditto, happened to me too.  Turned out the cable sleeve was broken allowing the wire inside to buckle.  Sometimes it would go smoothly other times it would buckle and not go into gear.  Happened at the track on day.  Try a wrecking yard first before you spend $150 on a new one.||||reg||1
